TwoStage_opamp_netlist

*p045_TT contains electrical models of Mosfets used in the circuit.
*45nm technology 
*Typical-Typical process corner (nominal NMOS and PMOS characteristics)

.include "ngspice_interface/files/spice_models/p045_TT.sp"    

*************************************************************************************

*.param means paramater in spice which is used to define a variable and assign a value to it.
*define it once and use it in multiple places, in transistor definitions below.

.param wp1=0.5u lp1=90n mp1=10    
.param wn1=0.5u ln1=90n mn1=38
.param wn3=0.5u ln3=90n mn3=9
.param wp3=0.5u lp3=90n mp3=4
.param wn4=0.5u ln4=90n mn4=20
.param wn5=0.5u ln5=90n mn5=60
.param cap=3p
.param res=1k

.param ibias=30u
.param cload=10p
.param vcm=0.6

.param VDD=1.2
.param temp_pvt=25
.param trf=0.5u ; for slew-rate calculation
.param period=10u ; for slew-rate calculation
.param vhigh=VDD ; for slew-rate calculation

*************************************************************************************

*mos_name drain gate source bias type w l m 
*circuit topology

mp1 net4 net4 VDD VDD pmos w=wp1 l=lp1 m=mp1     
mp2 net5 net4 VDD VDD pmos w=wp1 l=lp1 m=mp1
mn1 net4 net2 net3 net3 nmos w=wn1 l=ln1 m=mn1
mn2 net5 net1 net3 net3 nmos w=wn1 l=ln1 m=mn1
mn3 net7 net7 VSS VSS nmos w=wn3 l=ln3 m=mn3
mn4 net3 net7 VSS VSS nmos w=wn4 l=ln4 m=mn4
mp3 net6 net5 VDD VDD pmos w=wp3 l=lp3 m=mp3
mn5 net6 net7 VSS VSS nmos w=wn5 l=ln5 m=mn5
cc net5 net8 {cap}
rc net8 net6 {res}

ibias VDD net7 ibias

Vicm VCM VSS dc=vcm   
*Establishes common-mode voltage around which the input signals fluctuate.

*************************************************************************************

*Defines input voltage source
*DC voltage =0, Small-signal AC Amplitude = 1V, Pulse = Defines transient input waveform.
*Pulse = V1 : Initial Voltage, V2 : Final Voltage, TD :Time delay, TR : Rise Time, TF : Fall Time, PW : Pulse Width, Per : Period

Vinput aid VSS dc=0.0 ac=1.0 PULSE({-VHIGH/2} {VHIGH/2} {trf} {trf} {trf} {0.5*period-trf} {period})

*************************************************************************************

*voltage-controlled voltage source
*ename net1 VCM aid 0 0.5

ein1 net1 VCM aid 0 0.5
ein2 net2 VCM aid 0 -0.5

*************************************************************************************

*Power supply conenction

vdd VDD 0 dc=VDD
vss VSS 0 dc=0

*************************************************************************************

*Load Capacitor

CL net6 0 {cload}

*************************************************************************************

* set temperature

.temp {temp_pvt}

*************************************************************************************

* The .control tells NGSpice that the following commands are simulation-control commands.

.control
run
set units=degrees   *use degree instead of radians when giving phase related data
set wr_vecnames     *use vector names/column headers when writing data into output files.
option numdgt=7     *number of significant digits when printing numerical results

*************************************************************************************

* transient analysis : Shows how circuits voltage and current change over time when an input signal is applied.
*Transient analysis : mainly needed for slew rate computation
*Here, we can observe, how op-amp output responds to input pulse.
*Time step = 50ns and total simulation duration = 30us
tran 50n 30u

* save Vout data in a file named 'tran_TwoStage.csv'
*wrdata - write simulation data   , output folder,  File name,  voltage at the opamp output node.

wrdata ngspice_interface/Simulation_Result/tran_TwoStage.csv v(net1) v(net2) v(net6)

*************************************************************************************

* ac analysis  : Tells us how amplifier responds to input signals of different frequencies.
* This is important for measuring Gain, UGBW and Phase Margin
* ac simulation, decade by decade, 10 frequency points per decade from 1Hz to 1THz
* save Vout data in a file named 'ac_TwoStage.csv'
* This saves 2 important quantities : output voltage magnitude in decibels and output voltage phase in degrees.

ac dec 10 1 1T
display
wrdata ngspice_interface/Simulation_Result/ac_TwoStage.csv vdb(net6) vp(net6)

*************************************************************************************

* noise analysis
* calculate the output noise and save it in a file named 'noise_TwoStage.csv'
*.noise V(output) input_source dec points start_freq stop_freq
*onoise_spectrum - output noise spectral density v/s frequency
*inoise_spectrum - input noise spectral density v/s frequency

noise v(net6) Vinput dec 10 1 1T
wrdata ngspice_interface/Simulation_Result/noise_TwoStage.csv onoise_total


*************************************************************************************

* dc analysis
*calculate the operating point
*ngspice calculates the DC conditions of your circuit.
*DC Voltage at every node, DC Current through transistors and other circuit elements
*DC Operating conditions of the mosfets.

op

* save the total current consumption in a file named 'dc_TwoStage.csv'
wrdata ngspice_interface/Simulation_Result/dc_TwoStage.csv i(vdd)

*************************************************************************************

*end control
.endc

*************************************************************************************

.end

*************************************************************************************